  "texts": {
    "preamble": "P.Ganesh vs Ksrtc on 16 February, 2024 Kabc020217172021 In The Court Of The Iv Addl. Small Causes And Addl. Mact., Bangalore, (Scch-6) Present: Smt. Chetana S.F. B.A., L.L.B., Iv Addl., Small Cause Judge & Acmm, Court of Small Causes, Bengaluru. Dated This The 16th Day Of February 2024 M.V.C.No.3536 Of 2021 P.Ganesh S/o M.Prakash Aged about 38 years R/at # 101/3 Munibairappa garden Old Baiyappanahalli Maruthi Sevanagar Bengaluru560 033 Karnataka .. Petitioner (By Sri.S.Asha Adv.) Versus The Managing Director, Ksrtc 2 Mvc No.3536/2021 Judgment",
    "facts": "This is a petition filed u/s 166 of Indian Motor Vehicles Act and Rule 232 of Karnataka Motor Vehicles Rules claiming for compensation of Rs.50,00,000/ with interest from respondent on account of injuries sustained by the petitioner in the road traffic accident. 2. The petitioner's case in brief: That on 2672021 at about 11 a.m. when the petitioner was traveling on a two wheeler bearing reg.NO.KA 03ER2158 on Hosur road, near Hosa road junction bus stop, electronic city, at that time, driver of the KSRTC Bus bearing reg.No.KA 42F2148 came in negligently and stopped in the centre of the road and conductor P.Ganesh vs Ksrtc on 16 February, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/198602980/ 1 of the bus opened the door suddenly without caring for human safety and dashed against the petitioner, as a result of which JUDGMENT petitioner fell down and sustained injuries and took treatment at hospital. It is further stated that petitioner spent more more amount towards hospitalization, medicine etc., The petitioner was working as a carpenter and earning Rs.25,000/p.m. and due to accidental injuries, he lost his income and suffering from physical and mental stress. Hence prays to award compensation of Rs.50 lakhs from the respondent. 3. The respondent appeared through its counsel and filed written statement. In the written statement respondent contended that at Hosa road bus stop the driver of the bus stopped on the extreme left side of the road in order to get in the passengers, at that time, petitioner who himself came on his two wheeler in a rash and negligent manner, endangering to human life without observing the traffic rules and regulations, he himself knocked to the KSRTC bus door fell down and sustained injuries. The compensation claimed by the petitioner is excessive, exorbitant, unreasonable and speculative in nature. Hence prays to dismiss the claim JUDGMENT petition.",
    "arguments": "In the decision reported in AIR 2009 SC JUDGMENT 2819 (Bimla Devi & others V/s Himachal Road Transport Corporation & others), it has been held that in a Road accident, the strict principles of proof as in a Criminal case are not attracted. Relevant portion of the said decision is reproduced as follows: \"15. Be that as it may, the law is well settled that it is the impact of the physical disability on the particular avocation of the petitioner which is relevant for the purpose of assessment of compensation under the head of loss of future income as held by the Hon'ble Apex Court in Rajkumar's case reported in (2011) 1 SCC 343.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": "In the decision reported in AIR 2009 SC JUDGMENT 2819 (Bimla Devi & others V/s Himachal Road Transport Corporation & others), it has been held that in a Road accident, the strict principles of proof as in a Criminal case are not attracted. Relevant portion of the said decision is reproduced as follows: \"15. Be that as it may, the law is well settled that it is the impact of the physical disability on the particular avocation of the petitioner which is relevant for the purpose of assessment of compensation under the head of loss of future income as held by the Hon'ble Apex Court in Rajkumar's case reported in (2011) 1 SCC 343."
  },
